const e="ptu-zonal-youth-festival",u=2018,t="Read all 19 pages of the 'Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals' for session 2018-19 (Zonal and Inter Zonal), the document the template cites. No newer rulebook could be obtained: the university website (ptu.ac.in) refused the connection from this machine, and a web search found only later notices (2022 to 2026 venue and date lists and consent letters for host colleges) and no rulebook. Check the Department of Youth Affairs for a newer edition before use. The rules print no festival dates, venue or contact person or phone number, so the dates and venue are Variables saying 'not printed'. The rules print points for solo and group events but do not say which items are solo and which are group, so the points are written once under key 'points'. The rules do not print the languages of Vaar Singing or Folk Song (the Folk Song item names the Punjabi Folk Song category); Mimicry, Skit and One Act Play print English, Punjabi and Hindi, and Creative Writing prints English, Hindi and Punjabi (Urdu is printed only for Elocution, Debate and Poem Recitation). The Classical Dance time is printed as 12 to 15 minutes in the item list and as a maximum of 15 minutes in the item details; both are written. The 'Entry per institution' count is 1 in every item. The Debate time is printed as 4 to 5 minutes for each participant. The theme 'Youth Against Drugs' is the 2018-19 theme and is kept as a Variable.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"I.K. Gujral Punjab Technical University Zonal and Inter Zonal Youth Festival. Rules for colleges and students.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Theme: {{FestivalTheme}}. Every team must register each event before the due date on the host college portal or by email. A college that comes to the venue without registering on the portal pays a fine of {{OnTheSpotFine}}. Ages and student status are checked, and a student who is not eligible debars the team for 2 years.","Notes":["Dates and venues are not printed in the rules. Check with the host college and the Department of Youth Affairs.","Bring your College or Institute identity card. All participants must show it before taking part."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The theme of the festival is {{FestivalTheme}}. Think carefully about it when you prepare your events.","The rules follow the Inter-University Youth Festival rules of the Association of Indian Universities (AIU).","The material and instruments needed for an item can be brought or arranged by the team.","Proper screening must be done by the Cultural Coordinator or college authorities of the participating college before the team, contingent, participants and events are final.","Multi-talented students should be encouraged.","The host college gives only general light and spot lights on the stage. No extra lighting is allowed.","The Coordinator Cultural Affairs of the university ({{DepartmentOffice}}) can delay, postpone or bring forward an item or the festival because of unavoidable circumstances.","The Youth Festival continues despite the result of an objection or any other matter. Under no circumstances is the festival stopped.","The organising secretary has no right to stop any participant or team from taking part. This right lies only with the university officials and the observer of the Youth Festival."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Who Can Enter","Items":["Taking part is open to all bonafide full-time students enrolled in colleges affiliated with the university for an undergraduate or post-graduate degree of at least one academic year, whose examination is conducted by the university.","To identify a student, the manager of the participating team must give these documents: the 10th/Matric certificate, the 10+2 certificate, the graduation certificate for post-graduate students, and a photo identity card attested by the principal (the photograph is also attested by the principal).","Not more than 7 years may have passed since the student passed the examination that qualified them for first admission to a degree course of a university or affiliated college.","The age limit is up to 25 years on {{AgeLimitDate}}.","A full-time employee, lecturer, commercial artist or full-time artist of A.I.R., television or film is not allowed to take part.","A student cannot represent more than one college or institution, as participant or accompanist, during one academic year.","Provisional admission to a course of a university or college does not make a student eligible to represent the college or institution.","Under AIU rules, Ph.D. students are not eligible.","If a student sent admission forms to more than one college in the same session in the normal admission dates, they can take part from the college where they now study and attend classes, and from which the registration was sent to the university.","Every participant must show the College or Institute identity card before taking part.","The whole contingent from each college, university campus or institution must be under the overall charge of one coordinator or teacher as Contingent In-charge."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Register each event before the due date on the website portal of the host college, or by email. On-the-spot entries are discouraged.","A college that does not log in its data on the portal and comes directly to the venue on the first day of the festival pays {{OnTheSpotFine}}.","Send the individual Performa of each student, filled in and attested by the college Principal or Director, with the entry form. Two photographs of each student, attested by the Principal or Director, may be attached.","If any statement or fact in the entry form is wrong, the college Principal or Director is responsible.","The Principal or Coordinator must make sure the entry form is filled in properly and all details are correct.","The Department of Youth Affairs is not responsible if the entry form is not received by the department or the host college by the due date. An entry form received after the due date is not considered.","The list of all students taking part in the different items, with an authority letter, can be given to the host college during or before the managers' meeting. The list must be attested by the college Principal or Director.","Changes in entries can be made until the managers' meeting before the actual date of the festival.","The draw of lots for all events is done during the managers' meeting, as per the schedule. Teams compete in the order of the lots drawn.","Each team in an item is called by its institution code name or number. Only three calls are given. If the team does not report at the stage, it loses its right to compete. The next team is then called, and so on.","The team in-charge must keep teams ready according to the announcement made from the stage only. If there is a major problem, prior permission from the Coordinator Cultural Affairs is a must."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Fines","Items":["Every participating team pays an entry fee. {{ZonalEntryFee}}.","The fee is used by the host college to run the festival.","Fine for a college that does not log in its data on the portal and comes directly to the venue: {{OnTheSpotFine}}.","Fine for a team that does not take part in an event after confirming its entry in the managers' meeting: {{NonParticipationFine}}.","Fee for an objection: {{ObjectionFee}} (see Complaints)."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["{{FestivalDates}}","Changes in entries can be made until the managers' meeting before the actual date of the festival."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The festival is held at the host college of each zone: {{Venue}}.","Only these persons can stay in the festival campus: Principals and Directors, participants, accompanists, teachers or coordinators, and the Contingent In-charge."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entries from a College","Items":["Each institution can enter one team or participant in each item.","Change of one participant is allowed in group items when a college or institute qualifies from the Zonal to the Inter Zonal Youth Festival."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Zonal, Inter Zonal and Inter-University","Items":["In the Zonal Youth Festivals, performances of individuals and teams are judged only as 1st, 2nd and 3rd in all items. They qualify for the Inter Zonal Youth Festival.","In the Inter Zonal Youth Festivals, performances are judged only as 1st, 2nd and 3rd in all items.","University teams for the Inter-University Youth Festivals are chosen by the Department of Youth Affairs from the position-holder teams of the Inter Zonal Youth Festival, from versatile students. The decision is taken only by the Department of Cultural Affairs or the higher authority of the university.","The entry fee is payable only at the Zonal youth festivals."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Trophies","Items":["The award of trophies is decided on the total points scored by the team.","Solo events: first place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point.","Group events: first place 10 points, second place 6 points, third place 2 points.","Punjabi Folk Dance (Bhangra and Giddha) and One Act Play: first place 15 points, second place 10 points, third place 5 points."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards and Trophies","Items":["Medals and certificates are given to the 1st, 2nd and 3rd positions only, at both the Zonal and the Inter Zonal Youth Festivals.","Overall Winner Teams: the 1st and 2nd teams of the Zonal Youth Festivals are awarded trophies. The 1st and 2nd teams of the Inter Zonal Youth Festivals are awarded trophies.","Best Actor is declared with the result of the One Act Play. Best Dancers are declared in Bhangra and Giddha.","Best Speaker in all literary events (combined) is declared at each Zonal and Inter Zonal Youth Festival."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct","Items":["Fire arms and fire on the stage are strictly prohibited during any event and during the whole festival.","Disciplinary action is taken against any team, institution or team member who uses objectionable words against the judges, university officials or the Coordinator Cultural Affairs.","No participant or official of any institute may go to court or to the press on any controversial issue.","If a student is found ineligible during the festival days, the college team is debarred for 2 years.","If a member of an inter-college team is proved to be impersonating another student, or their admission in that college is proved to be fake, the whole team of that event is debarred from further participation in that Youth Festival.","The team of that college is also debarred from taking part in that event for the next two years, and the disciplinary committee appointed by the competent authority can impose a fine.","The cultural coordinator of that college is held responsible for sending the team. Strictures are sent against him or her to the college for action by the college management.","In theatre items, negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging, Time Limits and Results","Items":["Performance must not be less than the minimum time and must not exceed the maximum time for the item.","Grace time: 15 seconds for solo events and 30 seconds for group events.","The judgment of items is declared immediately after the event is over. The result is declared by the judges of the event."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Objections and Appeals","Items":["An objection is accepted only while the judges are in their seats, and only on a violation of the rules.","The objection is submitted by the Principal or an authorised teacher, with a fee of {{ObjectionFee}}. The fee is not refunded unless the objection is proved to be true.","If the objection against a team is found true, the team or participant is disqualified for that academic session.","If any dispute arises during the Inter-College Youth Festival, it is decided by the observer, and the decision is final. The university sends an observer with enough experience.","If any objection or problem is raised during the festival, a panel of jury solves it: the Observer of the Youth Festival appointed by IKG PTU, the Director or Principal of the host college, and the senior-most Principal or Contingent In-charge present.","The final appellate authority in any case is the Hon'ble Vice-Chancellor."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 (PDF)","Url":"https://www.gjimt.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Rules-_-regulations-for-PTU-Zonal-Youth-Festival-2018-19.pdf"}]}`),i=[],o=[],a=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Classical Instrumental (Percussion)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.7","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Taal, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Taal, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental (Non-Percussion)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.7","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.","Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian Raga system are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Use of Casio."],"Judging":["Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n- Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian Raga system are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Use of Casio.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Classical Vocal (Solo)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.7","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.","Take enough thought and care in the choice of raga and composition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film, cinema or recorded songs."],"Judging":["Voice, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n- Take enough thought and care in the choice of raga and composition.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film, cinema or recorded songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Voice, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Light Vocal Indian","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.7","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2."],"Allowed":["Only non-filmy, non-recorded songs, geet, gazal and abhangas.","Harmonium, Dholak and Tabla."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Voice, Swar, Taal, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only non-filmy, non-recorded songs, geet, gazal and abhangas.\\n- Harmonium, Dholak and Tabla.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Voice, Swar, Taal, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Folk Song","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.8","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The category for participation is Punjabi Folk Song."],"Allowed":["Non-filmy, non-recorded songs."],"NotAllowed":["Tabla and Keyboard."],"Judging":["Voice, Swar, Taal, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The category for participation is Punjabi Folk Song.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Non-filmy, non-recorded songs.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Tabla and Keyboard.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Voice, Swar, Taal, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Group Song Indian","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.8","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","A team presents two songs: one Patriotic song and one Folk song.","The group songs are taken from Indian songs, which can be in a religious language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film or recorded songs."],"Judging":["Singing, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- A team presents two songs: one Patriotic song and one Folk song.\\n- The group songs are taken from Indian songs, which can be in a religious language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film or recorded songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Singing, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Group Shabad/Bhajan","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.8","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 6. Time: up to 8 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","Only a non-film Indian language Bhajan or Shabad can be presented."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Singing, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 6. Time: up to 8 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- Only a non-film Indian language Bhajan or Shabad can be presented.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Singing, Swar, Taal, selection of Raag, composition and general impression, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.8-9","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","Language of the songs: English only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Singing, composition, rhythm coordination and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 6 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 2 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- Language of the songs: English only.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Singing, composition, rhythm coordination and general impression."},{"Title":"Western Group Song","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.9","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","Language of the song: English only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The quality of singing only, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team.","No weightage is given to dance during the performance."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- Language of the song: English only.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The quality of singing only, and not make-up, costumes and actions of the team.\\n- No weightage is given to dance during the performance."},{"Title":"Vaar Singing","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.9","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 2. Time: up to 7 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","A student can play an instrument and sing in place of a professional accompanist, but then the total number of participants is 4.","A Vaar is only in traditional verse forms.","Only heroic deeds of prominent patriotic personages of Indian history can be the subject of Vaar singing."],"Allowed":["Only traditional folk instruments of Punjab."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 2. Time: up to 7 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- A student can play an instrument and sing in place of a professional accompanist, but then the total number of participants is 4.\\n- A Vaar is only in traditional verse forms.\\n- Only heroic deeds of prominent patriotic personages of Indian history can be the subject of Vaar singing.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only traditional folk instruments of Punjab."},{"Title":"Bhangra","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.10","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.","The time is counted from the first beat of the Dhol."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 5.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","Only one form of Punjabi Folk Dance (male), that is Bhangra, is allowed in this category.","Actions follow the traditional forms of Dhol rhythm such as Bhangra, Luddi, Dhamal, Mirza, Jhumar, Pathania and Sialkotia.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.","The Boli singer can be a professional singer.","A Best Dancer is declared in Bhangra.","Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third)."],"Allowed":["Double and triple standing."],"NotAllowed":["Acrobatic actions."],"Judging":["Rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n- The time is counted from the first beat of the Dhol.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 5.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- Only one form of Punjabi Folk Dance (male), that is Bhangra, is allowed in this category.\\n- Actions follow the traditional forms of Dhol rhythm such as Bhangra, Luddi, Dhamal, Mirza, Jhumar, Pathania and Sialkotia.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n- The Boli singer can be a professional singer.\\n- A Best Dancer is declared in Bhangra.\\n- Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third).\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Double and triple standing.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Acrobatic actions.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."},{"Title":"Giddha","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.10","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 11. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.","The time is counted from the first beat of the Dholak or when the participants start singing, whichever is earlier."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 1.","Only the student participants sing the bolies.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.","A Best Dancer is declared in Giddha.","Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third)."],"Allowed":["Only plastic or metal bangles."],"NotAllowed":["Dhol.","Indecent or obscene bolies."],"Judging":["Variety of actions, their coherence with rhythm, symmetry, composition of the performance, and general impression such as grace and fitting expressions."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 11. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n- The time is counted from the first beat of the Dholak or when the participants start singing, whichever is earlier.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 1.\\n- Only the student participants sing the bolies.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n- A Best Dancer is declared in Giddha.\\n- Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third).\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only plastic or metal bangles.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Dhol.\\n- Indecent or obscene bolies.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Variety of actions, their coherence with rhythm, symmetry, composition of the performance, and general impression such as grace and fitting expressions."},{"Title":"Classical Dance (Exhibition Event)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.6 and 10","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: the list of items prints 12 to 15 minutes and the item details print a maximum of 15 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","The Classical Dance can be from any approved school of dance such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat-Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam and Odissi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Dance on a recorded cassette."],"Judging":["Taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, innovation, footwork and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: the list of items prints 12 to 15 minutes and the item details print a maximum of 15 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- The Classical Dance can be from any approved school of dance such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat-Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam and Odissi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Dance on a recorded cassette.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, innovation, footwork and general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Folk Dance (Exhibition Event)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.11","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.","The time is counted from the first beat, action, singing or voice of the instrument."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 5.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.","Only one form of Indian dance is allowed. A dance form from any state of the Indian Union is allowed except dance forms from Punjab.","Actions follow the traditional forms of that state's dance.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Dance on recorded music."],"Judging":["Rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n- The time is counted from the first beat, action, singing or voice of the instrument.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 5.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants, do not lead the performance and wear a different dress from the participants.\\n- Only one form of Indian dance is allowed. A dance form from any state of the Indian Union is allowed except dance forms from Punjab.\\n- Actions follow the traditional forms of that state's dance.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Dance on recorded music.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."},{"Title":"International Folk Dance (Exhibition Event)","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.12","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 5.","Only international student participants are allowed in this event.","Preference is given to international students as accompanists too.","A group can have all boys, all girls or both together, but a mixed team is allowed only if the folk dance form allows it.","The instruments should preferably be the folk or traditional instruments of that country.","The costumes should be the traditional or folk dress.","There must be no vulgarity or obscenity in actions, costumes or words.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.","Take enough thought and care that the item is not injurious to the personal or religious sentiments of any individual, community or nationality.","Participation certificates are given only to international student participants and accompanists."],"Allowed":["Dance on recorded music."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 10. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage or instruments: up to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 5.\\n- Only international student participants are allowed in this event.\\n- Preference is given to international students as accompanists too.\\n- A group can have all boys, all girls or both together, but a mixed team is allowed only if the folk dance form allows it.\\n- The instruments should preferably be the folk or traditional instruments of that country.\\n- The costumes should be the traditional or folk dress.\\n- There must be no vulgarity or obscenity in actions, costumes or words.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n- Take enough thought and care that the item is not injurious to the personal or religious sentiments of any individual, community or nationality.\\n- Participation certificates are given only to international student participants and accompanists.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Dance on recorded music."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.13","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (follow only one language).","The item is prose or poetry and not a song.","The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the competition.","The performance is judged in one language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Paper reading."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (follow only one language).\\n- The item is prose or poetry and not a song.\\n- The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the competition.\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Paper reading."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.13","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 2. Time: 4 to 5 minutes for each participant."],"Rules":["Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (the team follows one language).","Each institution is represented by two debaters: one speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST.","The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the competition.","The performance is judged in one language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Paper reading."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 2. Time: 4 to 5 minutes for each participant.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (the team follows one language).\\n- Each institution is represented by two debaters: one speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST.\\n- The subject or topic is announced 24 hours before the competition.\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Paper reading."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.13","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 3.","There is a written preliminary round. The 5 top position-holder teams go to the final round. There can be more than 5 teams if there is a tie.","The final round is oral, with audio-visual questions."],"Rules":["The Quiz Master gives the specific rules on how answers are judged, the time to reply to an answer and the type of round before the competition starts.","The decision of the Quiz Master is final.","One round of the quiz is based on the theme of the Youth Festival: {{FestivalTheme}}."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 3.\\n- There is a written preliminary round. The 5 top position-holder teams go to the final round. There can be more than 5 teams if there is a tie.\\n- The final round is oral, with audio-visual questions.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The Quiz Master gives the specific rules on how answers are judged, the time to reply to an answer and the type of round before the competition starts.\\n- The decision of the Quiz Master is final.\\n- One round of the quiz is based on the theme of the Youth Festival: {{FestivalTheme}}."},{"Title":"Poem Recitation","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.14","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (follow only one language).","The poem must be self-composed. It must be poetry and not a song.","The performance is judged in one language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Paper reading."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Language: English, Punjabi, Hindi or Urdu (follow only one language).\\n- The poem must be self-composed. It must be poetry and not a song.\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Paper reading."},{"Title":"Creative Writing - Poem Writing","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.14","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.","Two hours are given for composition in each category."],"Rules":["Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.","Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).","The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Awards are given category by category."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.\\n- Two hours are given for composition in each category.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.\\n- Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).\\n- The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Awards are given category by category."},{"Title":"Creative Writing - Short Story Writing","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.14","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.","Two hours are given for composition in each category."],"Rules":["Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.","Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).","The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Awards are given category by category."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.\\n- Two hours are given for composition in each category.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.\\n- Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).\\n- The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Awards are given category by category."},{"Title":"Creative Writing - Essay Writing","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.14","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.","Two hours are given for composition in each category."],"Rules":["Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.","Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).","The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Awards are given category by category."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Creative Writing is one entry of 3 participants. An institution sends one participant for each category: Poem Writing, Short-Story Writing and Essay Writing.\\n- Two hours are given for composition in each category.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Themes for creative writing are announced on the spot.\\n- Language of participation: English, Hindi or Punjabi (follow only one medium).\\n- The depiction of the theme must not be injurious to the personal, religious or national sentiments of any individual or community.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Awards are given category by category."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.15","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi."],"Allowed":["Mimicking sounds of machines and speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Mimicking sounds of machines and speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.15","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage: 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity or bitter insinuations."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination."],"Judging":["Theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 6. Time: 8 to 10 minutes. Time to set the stage: 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity or bitter insinuations.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.15","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 6. Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 2."],"Allowed":["Background recorded music."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 6. Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 2.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Background recorded music.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.16","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: up to 9. Time: 25 to 30 minutes. Time to set the stage: 10 minutes.","The time is counted as soon as the curtain goes up or the team starts giving an introduction, whichever is earlier."],"Rules":["Maximum number of accompanists: 3.","Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi.","The empty stage to empty stage rule is followed strictly.","The participating team brings its own set, stage property and make-up material.","The host institute provides the lighting. No extra lighting is allowed.","The participating team must report to the officials or department at least two hours before the play.","Accompanists either speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music.","The play can be in prose or verse but must not be in musical form.","Take enough thought and care in the choice of the play, which must suit the occasion and the taste of a general student audience. A play alien to our traditions, culture and social life is not shown.","Best Actor is declared with the result.","Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Presenting a play that the same college presented at the Youth Festivals of the last 3 years."],"Judging":["Theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: up to 9. Time: 25 to 30 minutes. Time to set the stage: 10 minutes.\\n- The time is counted as soon as the curtain goes up or the team starts giving an introduction, whichever is earlier.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: 3.\\n- Language: English, Punjabi or Hindi.\\n- The empty stage to empty stage rule is followed strictly.\\n- The participating team brings its own set, stage property and make-up material.\\n- The host institute provides the lighting. No extra lighting is allowed.\\n- The participating team must report to the officials or department at least two hours before the play.\\n- Accompanists either speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music.\\n- The play can be in prose or verse but must not be in musical form.\\n- Take enough thought and care in the choice of the play, which must suit the occasion and the taste of a general student audience. A play alien to our traditions, culture and social life is not shown.\\n- Best Actor is declared with the result.\\n- Placings score 15, 10 and 5 points (first, second, third).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Presenting a play that the same college presented at the Youth Festivals of the last 3 years.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Negative portrayal of eunuch, blind, handicapped, deaf and dumb characters is discouraged. Try to present positive characters."},{"Title":"On the Spot Painting","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.17","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches."],"Rules":["The item is held on the spot on the given topic or subject.","The participant brings their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute."],"Allowed":["Oil, water, poster or pastel colours."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is held on the spot on the given topic or subject.\\n- The participant brings their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Oil, water, poster or pastel colours."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.17","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches."],"Rules":["The topic or theme is given on the spot.","The participant brings their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute."],"Allowed":["A multicoloured poster."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topic or theme is given on the spot.\\n- The participant brings their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A multicoloured poster."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.17","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches."],"Rules":["The item is held on the spot on the given topic or subject.","The collage must be made from old magazines.","The participant brings their own material such as paste. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Scissors."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is held on the spot on the given topic or subject.\\n- The collage must be made from old magazines.\\n- The participant brings their own material such as paste. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Scissors."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches."],"Rules":["The item is held on the given topic or subject on the spot.","The idea must be innovative and original.","The participant brings their own material. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Sheet size: 22 x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is held on the given topic or subject on the spot.\\n- The idea must be innovative and original.\\n- The participant brings their own material. Only the paper or sheet is given by the host institute."},{"Title":"Clay Modeling","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The item is held on the spot.","Topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot.","The participant arranges pure clay and the required material.","The item must be at least 10 inches in height, with a permitted variation of 5%."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is held on the spot.\\n- Topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot.\\n- The participant arranges pure clay and the required material.\\n- The item must be at least 10 inches in height, with a permitted variation of 5%."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Size: from 2 x 2 feet to 4 x 4 feet, with a permitted variation of 5%."],"Rules":["Only one medium is used: poster colours, flower petals, saw dust, pulses or rice, without pasting.","This art is known by different names in different regions, such as mandna, alpana, alekhan, kolam and rangoli. The medium and the form of expression can be free-hand, pictorial and descriptive.","Participants must make the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers.","The topic or theme is given on the spot by the judges."],"Allowed":["Accessories such as a sieve, spoon and scale."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes. Size: from 2 x 2 feet to 4 x 4 feet, with a permitted variation of 5%.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one medium is used: poster colours, flower petals, saw dust, pulses or rice, without pasting.\\n- This art is known by different names in different regions, such as mandna, alpana, alekhan, kolam and rangoli. The medium and the form of expression can be free-hand, pictorial and descriptive.\\n- Participants must make the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers.\\n- The topic or theme is given on the spot by the judges.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Accessories such as a sieve, spoon and scale."},{"Title":"On the Spot Photography","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.19","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The participant brings their own digital camera.","The camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest starts.","The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.","The organisers have all rights to use these pictures as and when they want.","Additional instructions are announced on the spot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.","Software such as Photoshop to enhance an image."],"Judging":["Impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participant brings their own digital camera.\\n- The camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest starts.\\n- The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.\\n- The organisers have all rights to use these pictures as and when they want.\\n- Additional instructions are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.\\n- Software such as Photoshop to enhance an image.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Mehndi","Source":"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.19","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Participants: 1, with 1 student accompanist. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The item is held on the spot on the given subject or idea.","Additional instructions are announced on the spot.","Participants bring their own material.","Mehndi can be applied on both sides of one forearm (to the elbow)."],"Allowed":["Only traditional Indian motifs."],"NotAllowed":["Arabian mehndi.","Glitter."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Participants: 1, with 1 student accompanist. Time: 2 hours and 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is held on the spot on the given subject or idea.\\n- Additional instructions are announced on the spot.\\n- Participants bring their own material.\\n- Mehndi can be applied on both sides of one forearm (to the elbow).\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only traditional Indian motifs.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Arabian mehndi.\\n- Glitter."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"FestivalTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Theme of the Youth Festival",Value:"Youth Against Drugs",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.2 (Theme of Youth Festival, Zonal and Inter Zonal, 2018)"},{Key:"FestivalDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Festival dates and zone venues",Value:"Not printed in the rules. The Department of Youth Affairs sets the dates and the host colleges.",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 (no date or venue is printed)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival venue",Value:{Name:"Host college of each zone (to be announced)",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.3 (host college)"},{Key:"AgeLimitDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which the age limit of 25 years is checked",Value:"1 July of the academic year",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.2 (up to 25 years on 1st July of the academic year)"},{Key:"ZonalEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Zonal entry fee",Value:"Rs. 300 per event for each participating team, up to a maximum of Rs. 5000, payable to the host college, only at Zonal youth festivals",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.3"},{Key:"OnTheSpotFine",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fine for a college that does not register on the portal",Value:"Rs. 10,000",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.3"},{Key:"NonParticipationFine",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fine for not taking part in a confirmed event",Value:"Rs. 1000 per event",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.3"},{Key:"ObjectionFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee for an objection",Value:"Rs. 1000",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.3"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Theme and notices printed in the rules",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"Theme of the 2018-19 Youth Festival: Youth Against Drugs",Text:"The theme of the Zonal and Inter Zonal Youth Festival for session 2018-19 is Youth Against Drugs. Think and prepare your events with this theme in mind. One round of the Quiz is based on the theme.",Url:""}],Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.2-3 and p.13"},{Key:"DepartmentOffice",Kind:"address",Label:"Department of Youth Affairs / Coordinator Cultural Affairs",Value:{Name:"Coordinator Cultural Affairs, I.K. Gujral Punjab Technical University",Address:"Jalandhar-Kapurthala Highway",City:"Kapurthala",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals 2018-19 p.4"}],l=[{Claim:"Every rule, fee, fine, time limit and award captured here is printed in the university's Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals for 2018-19.",SourceType:"Primary - I.K. Gujral Punjab Technical University, Department of Youth Affairs official 'Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals'",Source:"Rules & Regulations of Youth Festivals (Zonal and Inter Zonal 2018-19)",Url:"https://www.gjimt.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Rules-_-regulations-for-PTU-Zonal-Youth-Festival-2018-19.pdf"}],h={TemplateKey:e,Year:2018,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,u as Year,h as default};
